  "original_content": {
    "math_academy_id": "q-125460",
    "knowledge_point_id": "976e05d4-59a8-5a93-be2f-b22357f388b9",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating Circulation",
    "problem": "Calculate the circulation $\u0393$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$",
    "worked_solution": "The circulation $\u0393$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\u2032}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t) & =(\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }10\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =10(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =20\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
